{"author":{"id":"2f242a7e7f2592f8909954a77fabece74f6e8cc197182647ed3b15ea8e3878af"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791143852,"nonce":"zr1jioYgh4GVF7XMy7+BmV7FUYM=","title":"a macOS redraw comes without the platform having a pass","message":"Since e505c4a3afd470c814973a267e2b8dc5b0982799, requestRedraw on macOS sets a flag, and the next poll or wait returns RedrawRequested at once, without pumping. A loop that draws only on RedrawRequested and asks again (hlwindow's examples/gpu/Triangle.hx: wait(0.05), render, requestRedraw) then never pumps the platform. It gets no events, and the wgpu surface never yields a frame.\n\nscripts/gpu_test.sh native in hlwindow: 8d581e7 passes with 221 frames; 39adb4a presents 0.\n\nFix: a redraw asked for becomes due only after the platform's next pass (a pump, or the host's next turn), and a wait with one asked for pumps without waiting.","files":null}]}